307588","company_name":"Goreha","title":"Chief Technology Officer (all identities)","description":"<br><strong>What to Expect</strong><p><p style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"><span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;color:#2d2d2d;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;">Caspar Health is entering its next growth phase. Our digital care is becoming increasingly critical to clinic and hospital operations. At the same time, we are progressing towards medical-device obligations and expanding AI-enabled ways of working.</span></p><p style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"><span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;color:#2d2d2d;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;">As CTO, you will own Technology and Engineering at C-level. You will report to the CEO, lead Engineering with full functional and disciplinary responsibility and work as a peer to the CPO.</span></p><p style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"><span style="font-size:12pt;font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;color:#2d2d2d;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;">Your job is not to become the bottleneck or Caspar's most important individual technologist. You will build a strong leadership layer and an Engineering system that moves quickly with security, resilience and evidence. You will stay close enough to technology to judge important decisions, risks and AI-enabled development through current practice.</span></p><br><p style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"><span style="font-size:12px;font-family:'Open Sans', sans-serif;color:rgb(45,45,45);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;">This position is based in Germany and must be performed, living in Germany. Due to our current payroll and social security arrangeme