 own new business growth targets for Gridcog in Germany and Central Europe, delivering on a pre-agreed quarterly sales target.</p><p>You’ll also have a passion for the Gridcog mission, be a self-starter who is happy to work at pace in a fast growing startup, and enjoy collaborating with your colleagues globally. If this sounds like you, please read on!<br></p><h3>What you’ll do as part of our team</h3><ul><li>Contribute to Gridcog’s growth by winning new Project Developer accounts in Germany and Central Europe, in line with agreed company and individual targets. This includes managing and qualifying a pipeline of opportunities, targeting specific client accounts, managing client demo processes and closing opportunities.</li><li>Develop a strong understanding of the renewable energy project financing lifecycle in Germany and across Central Europe, positioning yourself to support leading companies in expanding their asset portfolios.</li><li>Share customer and market insights with the wider Gridcog team.</li><li>Build your personal brand in the German energy industry by attending events and supporting Gridcog marketing activity.</li><li>Follow and improve our commercial processes including keeping your pipeline and deal records up to date in our CRM.</li><li>Act as part of a global team, supporting your colleagues in pursuit of company-wide goals.</li><li>Learn from and contribute to a small but experienced and successful business development team, with exposure to complex deals and decision making.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h3>To be successful in this role you will have</h3><ul><li>Demonstrated success in a senior commercial role in energy. This could be in data, research or SaaS sales, or a background in power markets gained through experience in origination, project development or analytics.</li><li>A strong network in the German energy ecosystem, particularly with Developers and IPPs.</li><li>A good understanding of battery storage in the German market.</li><li>Demonstrable success in both hitting and exceeding objective targets.</li><li>Ambition, energy and commercial drive. You’ll be a self-starter, comfortable in ambiguity and willing to get stuck in – Gridcog is a dynamic startup environment.</li><li>Exceptional communication skills in German and English, with a strong sense of customer empathy; you build strong and enduring relationships with your clients and with your colleagues in London, Madrid, Melbourne and Perth.</li><li>A willingness to become an expert in the Gridcog software.<br></li></ul><h3>We’d also love it if you have</h3><ul><li>Familiarity with Flexible Connection Agreements, EEG, MiSpeL and AgNes.</li><li>Technical knowledge in more than one of the following areas: renewable energy, battery storage or wholesale energy markets.</li><li>Knowledge of the energy project financing cycle including project bankability and debt financing.</li><li>Demonstrated success in a B2B SaaS business.</li><li>Experience using different sales methodologies.</li><li>Startup experience.</li><li>Fluency in another European language.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Competitive remuneration package aligned with experience and skills.</li><li>Opportunity to help build our Berlin based team, with flexible working arrangements.</li><li>Be part of a high-performing team that values innovation and creative problem-solving.</li><li>Contribute to the decarbonisation of the world’s energy system.</li><li>Support for ongoing professional and personal development.</li><li>An annual all company retreat, our previous retreats were in Bali and Bintan Island.</li></ul><p></p><h3>Diversity and Inclusion</h3><p>We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team at Gridcog. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, as we believe an inclusive environment and diversity of perspective lead to innovation and success.</p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/gridcog/senior-business-development-manager-project-developers-berlin-207567","tags":["Sales","Computer Software","Customer & Sales"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Berlin, Germany","created_at":1791480023},{"slug":"senior-e-e-engineer-emc-and-compliance-ugv-platforms-munchen-476649","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Senior E/E Engineer EMC and Compliance, UGV Platforms (m/f/d)","description":"<a target="_blank" href="https://www.fernride.com/"><img style="width: 650px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/b8sbpn98trem3vs54lo7m8fynocgn4/Quantum-Systems-uebernimmt-Fernride-169FullWidth-1559f24-393125.avif" /></a><p style=";;"></p><p><strong>Quantum Systems is a leading European deep-tech company for unmanned systems across air, land and maritime domains.</strong> We develop and scale integrated hardware, software and AI-powered solutions for mission-critical operations. By combining autonomous platforms with intelligent software and AI, Quantum Systems enables customers to operate, understand and act across domains.</p><p style=";"></p><p>Join Quantum-Systems and help bring autonomous ground systems into real world operations. As Senior E/E Engineer EMC and Compliance, you will own electromagnetic compatibility across our UGV platforms, starting with our Mandrill UGV: from the grounding and shielding concept on the drawing board to the certificate that puts our vehicles on public roads and into military service. Your goal is one robust E/E design baseline that passes civil homologation (UN ECE R10) and military qualification (MIL-STD-461, AECTP 500) without costly redesign loops. </p><p style=";"></p><p>This is a senior engineer role with real ownership and room to grow. You build our EMC capability from the ground up, set the strategy, decide early in the design, and lead campaigns through to certification. You will work at the intersection of high power electronics, vehicle E/E, radios and mission payloads, autonomy compute, suppliers, test houses and authorities. As the platform family and team grow, this role can develop into leading our EMC and compliance function. </p><p style=";;"></p><h4><strong>What is your Day to Day Mission:</strong></h4><ul><li><p><em>EMC Strategy and Compliance Ownership</em></p><ul><li><p>Define and own the EMC and E3 compliance strategy for our UGV platforms, covering civil vehicle approval (UN ECE R10, E mark for vehicle and ESA) and military qualification (MIL-STD-461G, MIL-STD-464, AECTP 500 / AECTP 250, MIL-STD-1275).</p></li><li><p>Translate customer, NATO and national requirements into an EMC control plan, requirement matrix and test strategy, and keep them current as configurations evolve.</p></li><li><p>Act as the technical interface to accredited test houses, technical services, type approval authorities and defence customers during qualification and acceptance.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><em>EMC by Design</em></p><ul><li><p>Develop and integrate the grounding, bonding, shielding and harness concept for the complete vehicle, with special focus on high voltage and high power electronics: traction inverters, DC/DC converters, battery systems and chargers together with outstanding team of engineers</p></li><li><p>Run EMC design reviews for schematics, PCBs, harnesses, enclosures and connectors; specify filters, transient protection and shielding concepts.</p></li><li><p>Manage RF coexistence on a dense platform:  datalinks, GNSS, tactical radios and payload emitters working side by side without degrading each other.</p></li><li><p>Flow down EMC requirements to suppliers, run component level reviews and assess their test evidence.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><em>Test, Troubleshooting and Qualification</em></p><ul><li><p>Build our in house pre compliance lab (LISN, spectrum analyser, near field probes, current clamps, automated measurement scripts) so issues are found on the bench, not in the chamber.</p></li><li><p>Plan, witness and lead full compliance campaigns at component, subsystem and vehicle level; drive root cause analysis and verified fixes when tests fail.</p></li><li><p>Use simulation (e.g. FEKO, CST, LTspice) where it saves test iterations.</p></li></ul></li><li><p><em>Cross Functional Collaboration and Standards</em></p><ul><li><p>Work closely with payload integration, vehicle E/E, mechanical, autonomy and manufacturing teams so EMC is built in, not bolted on.</p></li><li><p>Create EMC control plans, test procedures, reports and qualification evidence, and turn lessons learned into internal EMC design rules for every future platform and payload.</p><p style=";"></p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=";"></p><br /><br /><h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong></h4><p style=";"></p><ul><li><p>Degree in Electrical Engineering, Information Technology, Electronics or a comparable technical field.</p></li><li><p>8+ years of EMC experience in automotive, commercial vehicle, rail, aerospace or <span style="color: #000000">defence</span>, including ownership of at least one product through formal qualification or type approval.</p></li><li><p>Deep knowledge of automotive EMC (e.g. UN ECE R10, CISPR 25, ISO 11452, ISO 7637, ISO 10605) and working knowledge of military EMC (MIL-STD-461; ideally MIL-STD-464, AECTP 500, DEF STAN 59-411 or VG 95370/95373). Strong automotive profiles willing to extend into the military world are very welcome.</p></li><li><p>Solid experience with EMC of high voltage and power electronics systems.</p></li><li><p>Practical measurement expertise at component and vehicle level, and the ability to set up and automate test systems (e.g. Python, Matlab).</p></li><li><p>Structured root cause analysis, ideally backed by methods such as Six Sigma, and audit ready documentation.</p></li><li><p>Confident communication with engineers, suppliers, test labs, authorities and military customers.</p></li><li><p>Fluent in German and English.</p></li><li><p>High ownership, focus on teamwork, pragmatic, and happy to work directly on vehicles and in the workshop.</p><p style=";"></p></li></ul><h4><strong>Your Benefits: </strong></h4><p style=";"></p><ul><li><p><strong>Direct impact: </strong>See your contributions rapidly integrated from cutting-edge research into industrialized products, flying in the field within short development cycles. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Culture &amp; Environment: </strong>A dynamic, fast-paced, and collaborative startup environment with flat hierarchies, efficient collaboration, and a strong emphasis on continuous learning opportunities. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Work-life Balance: </strong>We offer flexible work schedules, and 30 days of paid vacation each year to support your personal and professional life. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Lunch Benefit: </strong>We promote healthy eating and the well-being of our employees with a monthly lunch budget. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> We support your physical well-being with a company-subsidized eGym Wellpass membership, giving you access to thousands of gyms and sports facilities. </p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/quantum-systems-gmbh/senior-e-e-engineer-emc-and-compliance-ugv-platforms-munchen-476649","tags":["Engineering","high school coursework"],"job_types":["Full-time permanent","senior manager / supervisor"],"location":"München","created_at":1791480010},{"slug":"senior-it-security-specialist-gn-hamburg-303267","company_name":"Workidentity","title":"Senior IT Security Specialist (gn)","description":"<br><strong>Einleitung</strong><p><span style="font-size:18px;">Mehr Verantwortung. Mehr Einfluss. </span><br><strong>Standort: Hamburger Westen | Hybrid (60% remote)<br></strong><br>Du hast s