<li><strong><u>Software Drivers</u></strong> - You should be comfortable writing code in C and familiar with Linux kernel development, debugging tools, and automated test frameworks. With a strong background in computer science, electrical, electronic, or software engineering, and an interest in operating systems and embedded hardware, you will develop, debug, and optimize Linux (and MCU) device drivers, build and run automated tests through CI systems such as Jenkins, and work closely with cross-functional teams to enable reliable integration of commercial and consumer product platforms.</li>
<li><strong><u>System Test</u></strong> - You should be comfortable writing code in Python and familiar with object-oriented languages like C++. With a background in electrical, electronic, computer, or software engineering and an interest in embedded systems and hardware/software integration, you will develop and run automated functional, system, and stress tests on real hardware, from FPGA emulation through to silicon.</li>

</div><br><strong>Skills and Requirements:</strong><br><div>

<li>Enrolled in MEng or BEng in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electronics and Electrical Engineering or a related subject degree and on track for a 2:1 or better</li>
<li>Some experience with development/evaluation of signal processing</li>
<li>Good understanding of software development principles</li>
<li>Interest in Embedded Systems</li>
<li>Excellent problem-solving ability</li>
<li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills</li>

</div><br><strong>What to expect from your internship with Cirrus Logic:</strong><br><div>

