,"tags":["Data Science"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1791484815},{"slug":"talent-partner-london-122541","company_name":"Seccl","title":"Talent partner","description":"<h1><strong>Talent partner</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid role to be based in our Holborn, London or George Street, Edinburgh office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About us</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Seccl is the Octopus-owned embedded investment platform, on a mission to help more people invest, and invest well.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the infrastructure behind the next generation of investing. Our technology already powers some of the UK’s most ambitious fintechs, banks, financial advisers and wealth firms, with close to a million investors relying on Seccl-powered platforms. And we’re now expanding into Europe.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve got a proven product, strong momentum and big ambitions for what comes next: helping more household-name brands launch and scale investment propositions, entering new markets and replacing outdated investment infrastructure with technology that’s faster, simpler and built for scale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re proud to be part of Octopus, one of the UK’s most successful privately held investment and technology groups. That gives us the backing and long-term perspective to build something substantial, while keeping the pace and energy of a high-growth business. Seccl and Octopus are both B Corp certified and share a belief that profit and purpose should go hand in hand.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to help shape the future of investing in the UK and across Europe, you’ll be in good company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out the Seccl <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://seccl.tech/"><u>website</u></a> to see what we’re building and read more about our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://seccl.tech/about/"><u>mission</u></a> to shape the future of investments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a talent partner to join our talent team, reporting to our talent lead. We have an ambitious hiring plan and need an experienced talent partner who can help us bring great people into Seccl at pace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on delivery role. You’ll primarily support our Product and Engineering teams, owning roles from intake and sourcing through to interview, offer and close. Product and Engineering will be your core focus, but you’ll also pick up hiring across other teams as our priorities change.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll build trusted relationships with hiring managers and bring clear advice, market insight and constructive challenge. You’ll help teams make strong decisions and keep hiring moving, while recognising that hiring managers remain accountable for the final call.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Things move quickly here and plans change. You’ll need to be comfortable working with ambiguity, adapting your approach and switching focus without losing momentum. You’ll care about a high hiring bar and a brilliant candidate experience, while staying pragmatic about how we get there.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you’ll own</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delivering end-to-end hiring across a portfolio of roles, primarily within product and engineering, while flexing across Seccl when priorities change to support with non-technical roles of all levels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building strong candidate pipelines through direct sourcing, agency management, creative search approaches and thoughtful engagement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creating pace across every hiring process, spotting blockers early and keeping candidates and hiring teams moving</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partnering with hiring managers and leaders to clarify what they need, share market insight and support strong, evidence-based decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintaining a high hiring bar and an inclusive, engaging experience without adding unnecessary process or complexity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Using hiring data and day-to-day insight to improve delivery, sharing practical ideas with the talent lead and wider People team</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>This role’s for you if...</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong experience owning and delivering end-to-end recruitment across multiple live roles in a fast moving, scaling business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring genuine expertise in product and engineering hiring, with the technical understanding and market knowledge to work credibly with hiring teams. In addition, you will have just as much passion in hiring for non-technical roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a confident direct sourcer who knows how to find, engage and build relationships with strong candidates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re highly delivery-focused, organised and proactive, and you naturally create momentum without needing lots of direction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable with ambiguity and incomplete information, and can change direction quickly when business priorities shift</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can challenge constructively, stay pragmatic and judge when to advise, when to push and when to help a hiring manager move forward</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re happy to recruit outside your core specialism when needed. Experience in a fast-paced or scale-up environment would be valuable</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>This role isn’t for you if...</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re looking for a mainly strategic or project-based role. </strong>Most of your time will be spent actively delivering hiring and owning live roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You need priorities and processes to stay fixed. </strong>Our needs can change quickly, so you’ll need to adapt and make sensible calls without perfect information</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You prefer to stay within one recruitment specialism. </strong>Product and Engineering will be your focus, but you’ll pick up roles across Seccl when needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You see partnership as owning the final hiring decision. </strong>We want you to bring expertise and challenge, while enabling hiring managers to make the call and keep things moving</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You rely mainly on inbound applications or agencies. </strong>Direct sourcing and proactive pipeline building are important parts of this role</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What’s in it for you</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a generous mix of benefits designed around the things that matter to our people:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 <strong>A salary between £55,000 and £65,000</strong>, reviewed annually, plus a 6% employer pension contribution and life assurance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌴 <strong>27 days’ holiday plus bank holidays</strong>, your birthday off and paid dependant leave</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💙 <strong>Two volunteering days each year</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌎 <strong>The option to work abroad for up to six weeks a year</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌟 <strong>Secclbrate</strong>, our recognition programme offering flexible rewards including extra pay, additional holiday and increased learning budget</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏅 <strong>One-month paid sabbatical after eight years</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏥 <strong>Private medical insurance with AXA Health</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👪 <strong>Enhanced parental leave</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 <strong>MacBook and up to £500 towards your home office set-up</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📖 <strong>£750 annual learning budget</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌻 <strong>Health and wellbeing support</strong>, including free therapy through Wellness Cloud and mental health support through Headspace</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌱 <strong>Financial wellbeing benefits</strong>, including Octopus Money, the Octopus Share Incentive Plan and will writing through Octopus Legacy</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎁 <strong>Perkbox</strong>, with flexible points and a range of discounts and perks</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚲 Access to Cycle to Work and Octopus Electric Vehicle Leasing</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our culture</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We put people first and try hard to create an environment where people feel trusted, heard and able to do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value openness, curiosity and different perspectives. You’ll have the freedom to challenge how things are done, experiment with better ways of working and take real ownership of your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out our Glassdoor page for the latest reviews or our LinkedIn for company updates and insights from the team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Interview process</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interviewing is a two-way process. Our interviews are conversational, with plenty of time for you to get to know us and ask questions too.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First stage - </strong>screening interview with the talent lead</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Second stage -</strong> interview with the head of people and talent lead to delve into your technical skills via a case study/scenario based task</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final stage - </strong>45 mins bar-raiser culture-based interview with two key stakeholders for this role</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We review applications as they come in and may close the role once we have enough candidates to move forward. We’ll keep you updated throughout.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Everyone’s welcome</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want to build a diverse and inclusive company full of brilliant people with different skills, experiences and perspectives. All applicants will be considered without regard to age, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, veteran status, neurodiversity or disability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like your kind of thing, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t tick every box. <strong>We’d love to hear from you.</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: £55K – £65K</p><ul><li> • £55K – £65K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/seccl/talent-partner-london-122541","tags":["People"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1791484815},{"slug":"senior-full-stack-engineer-hawkai-budapest-73855","company_name":"Hawkeyeinnovations","title":"Senior Full Stack Engineer - (HawkAI)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join Our Team as a Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer (HawkAI) at Hawk-Eye Innovations</strong> <br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Hybrid working – minimum 2 days per week in the office</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Office:</strong> Budapest, Váci út 144-150, 1138 Hungary</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Contract:</strong> Permanent, Full-Time<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Hawk-Eye, we build technology that powers some of the most exciting and critical moments in sport, from instant replays and broadcast augmentation to officiating systems trusted by leagues, federations, broadcasters, and millions of fans worldwide.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our HawkAI team builds the foundational machine learning infrastructure that powers the future of sports intelligence. This is a build-from-zero role designed to bridge the gap between machine learning engineering and real-world application. You will be responsible for building the first-pass applications and services that sit on top of the HawkAI Engine, translating cutting-edge ML models and data pipelines into working, demonstrable software. If you thrive on autonomy, rapid execution, and leveraging modern AI-assisted workflows to build products from scratch, this is where you belong.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer who can comfortably navigate the entire stack to get credible first versions into the hands of users. You won't be handed a fully scoped brief; instead, you’ll work closely with ML engineers to figure out what a credible first pass looks like, making high-leverage architectural choices and proving out new product opportunities.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build-from-Zero Applications:</strong> Move across the entire stack to design, build, and deploy the first working software applications and services powered by the HawkAI Engine.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridge ML and Product:</strong> Translate complex ML models and real-time data pipelines into responsive, high-throughput APIs and intuitive user interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-Accelerated Development:</strong> Maximize your build velocity by deeply integrating modern AI-assisted and agentic development tools into your day-to-day workflow, while retaining strict human oversight on software architecture and data integrity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real-Time Visualization:</strong> Design and implement high-performance interfaces to stream and visualize 2D sports data with minimal latency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-End Delivery:</strong> Own the end-to-end lifecycle of early-stage applications, from cloud infrastructure (AWS) and CI/CD deployment to frontline delivery.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Versatile Full-Stack Expertise:</strong> Broad hands-on experience moving fluidly across backend, frontend, and deployment, specifically with Java, TypeScript, React, Node.js, Python, and modern responsive web technologies (HTML5/CSS3).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AWS &amp; Infrastructure:</strong> Demonstrated experience designing, building, and deploying end-to-end cloud solutions on AWS infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CI/CD &amp; DevOps:</strong> Proven capability deploying production-ready CI/CD pipelines using Docker and GitHub Actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data Streaming &amp; 2D Rendering:</strong> Experience streaming, processing, and visualizing dynamic data using 2D rendering engine tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ML Integration:</strong> Experience building APIs and microservices that integrate directly with ML models, keeping latency and throughput constraints front-of-mind.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pragmatic Quality:</strong> The ability to write high-quality, testable, and maintainable code that accounts for edge cases, even when executing at high speeds.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus Points For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with 2D rendering libraries like PixiJS or mobile frameworks like React Native.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with AWS SageMaker, AWS Bedrock, SQL, Redis/Valkey, or infrastructure-as-code using Terraform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with building or working alongside agentic AI systems.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What This Role Is Not</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Not an ML Engineering Role:</strong> You will work directly with ML engineers, but your focus is building product services on top of their models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Not a Fixed Roadmap Role:</strong> You won't execute against rigid specs; a key part of your initial phase is defining what the product should actually be.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Not a Management Role:</strong> This is a dedicated, high-impact individual contributor position.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Not a Long-Term Maintenance Role:</strong> You focus on turning 0 to 1; once opportunities are proven, dedicated teams scale and maintain them.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hungary Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual Leave:</strong> Standard according to local labour law.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible Working:</strong> Hybrid model (2 days in our Budapest office per week).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Access to Sporting Events:</strong> Priority access and tickets to major sporting events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sony Group Discounts:</strong> Generous discounts across Sony Group products and services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Other Benefits:</strong> Flexible Cafeteria options (SZÉP Card, Nursery &amp; Kindergarten contributions, Annual MOL Bubi Pass), Private Medical Insurance, Life &amp; Accident Insurance, MindentMent Dental Clinic discounts, Seniority Awards, and an Employee Assistance Program.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. Everyone is treated fairly, regardless of gender, race, religion, age, disability, or background. We want you to be your best and truest self here.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Apply Today</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re excited by the idea of shaping the future of sports technology through cutting-edge R&amp;D, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/hawkeyeinnovations/senior-full-stack-engineer-hawkai-budapest-73855","tags":["Hawk-Eye Innovations (Value Streams)"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Budapest, Hungary","created_at":1791484814},{"slug":"talent-acquisition-specialist-london-376448","company_name":"Bjak","title":"Talent Acquisition Specialist","description":"<h2>About BJAK</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The original mission of BJAK is we believe people deserve smarter ways to plan, save and grow their money. This is the origin of our name.<br /><br />Started in 2019, we built the first mobile-first, insurance platform, enabling insurance to be accessible online by millions in the region. Today, its the leading insurance platform in Southeast Asia.<br /><br />Today, we are expanding ways to help people in the region — this includes spending, saving, investing, exchanging, travelling, and more. Our mission is help people get more from their money every day.<br /><br />We have teams working around the world, with over 20 nationalities from our offices and remotely, who truly enjoys their work. We are looking for the most talented and driven people we can find. We are looking for people who work for their passion, not counting hours. Who loves building great next-generation products, not status quo. Who cares about redefining how everyone around us can get the best financial applications, not for an exclusive few.</p><h2><br />The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Talent Acquisition Specialist to support hiring across multiple functions and regions as BJAK continues to scale globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on recruitment role for someone who enjoys working in a fast-paced environment, managing multiple hiring priorities, and partnering closely with stakeholders to deliver hiring outcomes. You will have exposure to a wide range of functions including Operations, Finance, Marketing, Creative, HR, Product, Engineering, and other business-critical teams.</p><h2><br />What You’ll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage end-to-end recruitment processes for assigned roles across multiple functions and locations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with hiring managers to understand hiring needs, candidate profiles, and business priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source, screen, assess, and engage candidates through various channels including LinkedIn Recruiter, referrals, job boards, and direct outreach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain strong talent pipelines for both active and future hiring needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct talent mapping and market research to support hiring strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate and manage interview processes while ensuring a positive candidate experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate candidate records and recruitment activities within the Applicant Tracking System (ATS).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide regular hiring updates and pipeline insights to hiring managers and stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support recruitment process improvements, hiring initiatives, and employer branding activities where required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with recruiters, coordinators, and business leaders to achieve hiring goals across the organization.</p></li></ul><h2><br />The Right Fit Has</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2–5 years of experience in Talent Acquisition, Recruitment, Executive Search, Staffing, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience managing multiple vacancies simultaneously in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong sourcing capabilities across LinkedIn Recruiter, job boards, referrals, networking, and direct outreach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience recruiting across multiple functions such as Operations, Finance, Marketing, Creative, HR, Product, Engineering, or other corporate functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong candidate assessment and interviewing skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and stakeholder management abilities.</