siness, ideally a venture-backed scale-up, working directly with founders, engineers, and commercial teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Line-management or mentoring experience with junior counsel, paralegals, or secondees. Does not need to be extensive but needs to be real, and you want to manage and grow a team as the function scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with technical subject matter. You can get to grips with OLIX’s technology well enough to draft and negotiate around it credibly and to hold your own with engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI-native approach to legal work. You actively use AI tools in your day-to-day practice, have strong instincts for what AI does well and where it fails, and treat AI fluency as a core craft skill rather than a novelty.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bias toward building scalable systems over doing work manually. You look for the automation, template, or workflow that solves the problem ten times, not just once.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercially pragmatic, able to move at pace, and comfortable owning positions without constant supervision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct, plain-language communicator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The right fit for how OLIX works: hands-on, direct, high ownership, and comfortable being part of the team rather than a gatekeeper. You would rather solve the problem than write the memo.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in technology or in technical manufacturing more broadly, ideally B2B hardware, semiconductors, or infrastructure. Highly desirable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supply chain experience: supply, manufacturing, component, and logistics arrangements, and the issues that come with scaling a hardware supply chain (capacity and volume commitments, al