nto accurate notes, automatically, backed by ambient real time document creation, intelligent document management and clinical workflow automation, native patient data integrations across siloed health systems, and a patient and clinical communications layer. Thousands of clinicians across multiple disciplines use Lyrebird every day in environments where accuracy, safety, and time matter deeply. We're growing fast across Melbourne, the UK, and Asia, and there's a finite window right now to set the standard for clinical AI before anyone else does.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own recruitment end to end, from sourcing and headhunting through to offer, so every role closes with the right person at the pace our growth demands</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find and land niche, highly skilled people who aren't looking, building pipelines ahead of need so we never start from zero</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape hiring priorities, budgets, and workforce planning alongside leadership, bringing market insight that changes decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build an ATS and hiring process that moves candidates through the funnel fast, with no one waiting more than 12 hours for a response</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the standard for candidate experience, so every person who meets Lyrebird, hired or not, leaves feeling respected and dealt with honestly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver clear reporting and insight that keeps leadership aligned, accountable, and ahead of hiring risk</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI-powered systems and automations with Claude that remove manual work and make the whole function faster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead core UK people initiatives as our UK People Partner, working closely with our Head of People &amp; Culture in Australia</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of owning full-cycle recruitment and closing roles end to end, whether in-house, agency, or both</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven success headhunting hard-to-find talent, particularly people who weren't on the market until you found them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A deep network across tech start-ups and SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The judgement to hold a high quality bar while moving fast, and the rigour to keep process and detail tight under pressure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of partnering with senior leaders as a trusted advisor, not an order taker</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience recruiting inside a hyper-growth startup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience hiring for technical, product, or health-tech roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or rebuilding an ATS and recruitment reporting from scratch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A network across the Australian, UK, or Asian tech markets</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every engineer, clinician, and operator you bring in will help give doctors back hours of their day and put that time back where it belongs: with patients. The people you hire will decide how quickly Lyrebird reaches every clinician who needs it, and that's work you'll be able to point to for the rest of your career.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building a team that reflects the diversity of the people who benefit from our work. We want Lyrebird to be a place where everyone feels safe, supported, and able to thrive. If you're from an underrepresented background in tech, we strongly encourage you to apply, even if you don't meet every requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lyrebird-health/talent-people-partner-12-month-ftc-united-kingdom-420174","tags":["People & Culture"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1791474011},{"slug":"pre-sales-consultant-london-39377","company_name":"Vitesse","title":"Pre-Sales Consultant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are Vitesse – the treasury and payment partner of choice for insurance.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your next adventure awaits!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join the team who are redefining the payments space.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Vitesse, we're more than just a payments platform – we're the trusted financial infrastructure connecting the global insurance ecosystem. Tailor-made for insurers, brokers, MGAs, and TPAs, our unified platform optimises claims funds, enables real-time global payments, and delivers full financial control. Our impact is real: over $20 billion in payments across 200+ countries, hundreds of millions returned to insurers’ balance sheets, and counting. We’re licensed in the UK (FCA), Europe (DNB), and New York (NYDFS), with over 260 amazing colleagues worldwide. With $93 million recently raised in Series C funding from KKR, our journey is just beginning, and our ambitions are sky-high.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Headquartered in the heart of London and expanding across Europe and the US, Vitesse is where your ideas power tomorrow’s insurance solutions. Are you ready to make a difference? You're in the right place.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting into our Pre-Sales Lead, you will play a pivotal role in Vitesse’s sales and product development processes. You will partner with our sales, product, and engineering teams to deliver compelling, value-driven demonstrations and technical presentations. You will be responsible for understanding customer needs, positioning our solutions effectively, and driving engagement with prospects and partners. You will also collaborate closely with the product team to establish a continuous feedback loop, aligning current product functionality, upcoming feature releases, and customer requirements to drive product improvements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role requires a blend of technical expertise, consultative skills, and business acumen to help prospects and customers understand how our platform can solve their unique challenges.</p><h3>Responsibilities:</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading discovery sessions to gain a comprehensive understanding of our customers’ needs, business objectives, and internal operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participating in all stages of the sales lifecycle, including leading pitches, product demonstrations and technical workshops</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establishing continuous collaboration and feedback loops with Product Owners to ensure alignment with customer needs and product improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with each product team to ensure feature demos and product collateral support your needs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leveraging your deep functional and technical understanding of our products and their benefits, along with knowledge of our customers, you must be able to:</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carefully choose which aspects or benefits of our product to highlight/downplay in each customer engagement, ensuring the message resonates, and the customer is not overwhelmed with complexity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Propose (in consultation with the Product team) creative uses, adaptations, and customizations of our products to better meet individual customer needs (with a view towards reusability for future customers as well, as much as possible)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage and deliver relevant customer feedback to Product Ownership teams to aid in roadmap planning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with senior stakeholders to define the business value proposition, target audience, and competitive landscape</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure communications and sales collateral clearly explain the Vitesse value proposition and drive the right level of understanding and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to proposal development, working closely with sales and product teams to draft technical responses and customize solutions for potential clients.</p></li></ul><h3>Role requirements:</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working for a SaaS (Software as a Service) company is essential, having served the insurance industry is highly desirable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to demonstrate deep functional and technical understanding of an existing SaaS platform operating in the treasury, claims management, business card or high-value payments markets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience delivering value-centric presentations (virtually and in-person) directly to key decision makers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with sales teams and participating in all aspects of the sales cycle</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to influence stakeholders and key decision makers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work cross-functionally with product, sales, senior leadership, success, and solutions teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meticulous attention to detail, especially when creating external collateral (e.g. presentations, partner decks)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stellar organizational and time management skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience attending networking events, expos and trade shows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience presenting to large audiences and acting as an ambassador for the company and its solutions</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that everyone has their own work rhythm and believe in a flexible working schedule - at Vitesse you’re expected to work 35 hours a week. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Values – or what we call “Vitesse at Our Best”</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Vitesse values are a true reflection of what it takes to thrive in our business, so it’s important to us that any employee who joins our business is aligned with these 3 attributes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Confident Humility</strong> <br />We believe the best ideas come from listening and learning. We leave ego at the door, ask for help when we need it, and celebrate collective success. When one of us wins, we all do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Driven to Succeed</strong> <br />We’re ambitious about the opportunity ahead and committed to achieving it together. We hold ourselves to high standards, take pride in what we deliver, and push for meaningful outcomes for our customers, our partners, and each other.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tenacious Responsibility</strong> <br />We take ownership of our work, our decisions, and our results. We face challenges with resilience, learn from setbacks, and see things through to completion. Because doing the right thing matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We commit to creating an inclusive environment that enables everyone to perform at their best, where we recognise the rights of all individuals to mutual respect and where there is an unbiased acceptance of others. Our policies and practices aim to promote an environment that is free from all forms of unlawful or unfair discrimination and values the diversity of all people. At the heart of our policy, we seek to treat people fairly and with dignity and respect<strong>. </strong>If you require any interview adjustments please contact Clara Moretti-Parker on <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="Hyperlink SCXW126046645 BCX8" ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/vitesse/pre-sales-consultant-london-39377","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1791474011},{"slug":"design-engineer-web-brand-old-street-95736","company_name":"Granola","title":"Design Engineer (Web & Brand)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Hey! We’re team Granola 👋</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you haven’t already, you should check out <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.granola.ai/"><u>what we’re building</u></a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.granola.ai/jobs"><u>why you should work here</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Design Engineer to own how Granola shows up on the web and help people understand what it can do, what makes it special, and how to get started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll combine strong design instincts with front-end engineering skills, taking ideas from early exploration through to a live website. Your work will shape how people first encounter Granola, bringing the care and personality of our product to the pages that introduce it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want to build one of the best websites in the industry. That means making Granola’s story clear, giving every interaction care and attention, and building the foundations that let us keep improving as we grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the website’s development.</strong> Help set its direction, identify opportunities and take responsibility for the quality of what ships. Continuously improve the site’s SEO, performance and accessibility, keeping it fast, discoverable and easy for everyone to use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Push what a website can be. </strong>Set an ambitious creative and technical bar, and make Granola’s website one of the best product marketing experiences on the internet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring Granola’s story to life.</strong> Work with marketing and design on the homepage, feature pages, enterprise pages and other experiences that explain our product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep the everyday experience improving.</strong> Give navigation, pricing, calls to action and smaller updates the same attention as major launches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the infrastructure to help us move faster.</strong> Develop reusable components, page templates and CMS workflows that make publishing straightforward across the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support experimentation.</strong> Build campaign landing pages and enable A/B testing, using what we learn to improve the site.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your background looks something like:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and building websites, with work you can show us that demonstrates both visual judgement and technical ability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly proficient with React, TypeScript, Tailwind and have a solid grasp of modern frontend architecture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence taking work from an initial idea into production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An eye for typography, layout, hierarchy and interaction - and an understanding of how those choices help communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort exploring ideas in design tools and code, choosing whichever helps you make progress.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with reusable components, content management or publishing workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interest in websites as a creative discipline: helping people understand a product and giving them a reason to try it.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>How you work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy taking ownership, bringing ideas and following them through. You can move between a substantial redesign and a small improvement, applying judgement about where extra polish will make the biggest difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable collaborating with marketing, design and product colleagues, asking good questions about a brief and helping shape the solution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are living in the most exciting time for tool builders since <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mother_of_All_Demos">Engelbart's demo</a> in 1968. We want to assemble the best crew to build this future together, here in London. Our compensation philosophy is to pay slightly above market on salary and above market on equity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We do our best work in person, and so our team spends time together five days per week in ou