ory, capex, loan note, fx, etc.) and assisting with the preparation of monthly management reports. Assist with maintaining compliance with US and UK requirements, such as HMRC and IRS.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are in a new commercial phase in the business and expanding our functions outside of the UK so we are looking for someone who wants to grow and develop in this role and become familiar with finance across different geographies. A drive for continual efficiency, quality, and process improvements across all Finance team processes is necessary, as well as excellent attention to detail</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Key Accountabilities</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the financial accounting system with up to date and accurate data; maintain company travel platform; Maintain and update company wide approval system</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure expense claims are in line with policy and reviewed, approved and paid in a timely manner</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure customer invoices are raised promptly and customers are supported in delivering payment when due</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure suppliers are paid in line with contracted payment terms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preparation of month-end schedules and journals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Completion of balance sheet reconciliations on a quarterly basis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Banking platform management including transfers, investments, payments and refunds; tracking and management of banking reconciliations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compliance requirements such as ONS Surveys, and assistance with US tax matters</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continued process improvement identification</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Who You Are</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Core competencies, knowledge and experience:</stron