ch Check)</p></li><li><p>Flexible Arbeitszeiten und Orte&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Möglichkeit zum Ferienkauf, Sabbatical und Workation innerhalb der EU</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Klingt spannend? Du überzeugst uns mit deinem Lebenslauf, Arbeits- und Studien-zeugnissen sowie einem Motivationsschreiben. Darin kannst du uns gerne schon mitteilen, ab wann du zur Verfügung stehen würdest und mit welchem Pensum. Bei Fragen vorab melde dich jederzeit bei unserem Recruiting Team unter: <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>So geht es weiter: Wir werden deine Unterlagen intern prüfen und uns im Regelfall innerhalb einer Woche bei dir zurückmelden. Üblicherweise kannst du bei uns mit 2 Gesprächen rechnen, die an unseren BSI Standorten persönlich stattfinden. Anstelle von Assessments legen wir Wert darauf, uns gegenseitig kennenzulernen.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/bsi-software/remote-junior-cloud-operations-engineer-all-genders-ch-baar-284023","tags":["Services","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Homeoffice","created_at":1791394255},{"slug":"senior-manager-finance-accounting-advisory-us-markets-schweiz-zurich-234260","company_name":"Cfgigermany","title":"(Senior) Manager (f/m/d) Finance & Accounting Advisory - US Markets","description":"<br><strong>Key responsibilities</strong><p>You advise clients on the complex accounting and financial reporting matters that shape their most important decisions, including:<br><ul><li><strong>Subject matter expertise:</strong> Serve as the firm's subject matter expert for US GAAP reporting and US-related transactions, covering inbound and outbound deals as well as US filers.</li><li><strong>US transaction hub:</strong> Build and lead a local hub for US transactions, working closely with CFGI Americas to capture cross-border synergies (e.g. in the Biotech market).</li><li><strong>M&amp;A accounting:</strong> Shape the accounting and reporting that underpins major M&amp;A transactions – purchase accounting, combined financial statements, pro-forma financial information, and post-deal finance integration.</li><li><strong>Capital Markets &amp; IPO services:</strong> Guide companies to US capital markets, from IPO readiness and execution (including SEC reporting) through post-listing requirements.</li><li><strong>Technical &amp; operational accounting:</strong> Advise clients on conversions to US GAAP, consolidations, PCAOB audit-ready reporting and closing procedures, and implementation of new accounting pronouncements.</li><li>Lead engagements from first scope to final delivery – manage engagement economics, delivery risk, and stakeholder expectations.</li><li>You are a significant part of growing the Swiss practice – spotting opportunities within existing relationships, contributing to proposals, and building new business.</li><li>Add to the firm's voice through developing new service offerings, hosting events and preparing publications.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Required qualifications & attributes for success</strong><p>You will recognize yourself in most of the following:<ul><li>An academic background in accounting, finance, or economics, ideally paired with a qualified accountant credential (US CPA, ACCA or equivalent).</li><li>Six to eight years in a Big 4 or comparable advisory environment, or in a senior technical accounting or financial reporting role in industry.</li><li>Deep, applied knowledge in US GAAP (IFRS a plus), applied to complex standards in a client-facing or technical accounting setting.</li><li>Fluent in English.</li></ul>The qualities and skills that will take you furthest with us:<br><ul><li>The interpersonal skills to build trusted relationships with senior finance stakeholders (e.g. CFOs, controllers, audit committees, and external auditors, etc.).</li><li>Advisory experience with capital markets transactions, such as IPOs/de-SPACs and carve-outs.</li><li>Curiosity, a collaborative instinct, and the ambition to thrive somewhere entrepreneurial and growing fast.</li><li>A track record of leading several engagements at once, managing their economics, and delivering quality work under tight timelines.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Why join us</strong><p>We invest in our people and back it up with real benefits:<br><ul><li>Above-average compensation</li><li>Pillar 2 occupational pension plan with increased savings rates</li><li>25 vacation days</li><li>Flexible working</li><li>Reka-Lunch meal card</li><li>SBB half-fare travelcard</li><li>Mobile phone with a fully covered European carrier plan</li><li>Internal coaching program</li><li>Company events (office outings | quarterly events)</li></ul></p><br><strong>Privacy Notice</strong><p>By submitting your application, you are providing personal data to CFGI Germany GmbH, Theodor-Heuss-Straße 10, 70174 Stuttgart ("CFGI"). This is necessary in order for your application to be considered. CFGI processes the data you provide for the purpose of further reviewing your application.<br> <br>Please note that CFGI is part of the globally operating CFGI Group, which includes, in particular, companies in the United States (USA) and the United Kingdom (UK). The position advertised here involves an international scope of work and integration into international teams. This may require involving colleagues based outside the European Union already at the application stage. Your application documents will be made available electronically to colleagues with whom you will later work (in the USA and/or UK). CFGI always ensures an appropriate level of data protection in doing so.<br> <br>Your data will be processed exclusively for the purpose of the application process and will be deleted after the selection process is completed, in compliance with statutory retention periods. You also have the right to access, erasure, and data portability under Art. 20 GDPR, as well as, where applicable, the right to have incorrect data we process about you corrected. Likewise, you may object to the processing of your data by us and request that it be restricted.<br> <br><strong>Data Protection Officer</strong>:<br>heyData GmbH<br>Schützenstraße 5<br>10117 Berlin<br>Website: <a href="http://www.heydata.eu/" title="http://www.heydata.eu/">www.heydata.eu</a><br>E-Mail: <a ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/cfgigermany/senior-manager-finance-accounting-advisory-us-markets-schweiz-zurich-234260","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Schweiz (Zürich)","created_at":1791392957},{"slug":"senior-embedded-performance-engineer-zurich-349475","company_name":"Auterion","title":"Senior Embedded Performance Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;Auterion builds a cutting-edge operating system for autonomous robotic systems that empower a diverse range of platforms to perform surveillance, reconnaissance, inspection, mapping and logistics tasks. Our industry-leading software drives the adoption of robotic fleets and is recognized by the U.S. government as the future standard for its drone programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Embedded Performance Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; who is passionate about getting the most out of embedded systems — from low-level Linux tuning and hardware integration to high-performance video and data pipelines. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working close to hardware, moving across the stack, and solving the kinds of problems where milliseconds, bandwidth, startup time, and system efficiency matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the AuterionOS ecosystem on topics such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded Linux performance and system tuning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low-latency video streaming and media pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C/C++, Python, and Bash-based platform development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardware integration, system profiling, and end-to-end optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration with experienced and driven engineers across Auterion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within the Apps &amp;amp; Simulation team and collaborate with other development teams to build high-performance products for autonomous systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, optimize, and maintain performance-critical components within AuterionOS, Auterion’s custom embedded Linux distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve end-to-end system behavior across compute, networking, video, and hardware interfaces, with a strong focus on latency, throughput, reliability, and resource efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and optimize demanding workloads such as real-time telemetry, video streaming, media processing, and communication between distributed system components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate system bottlenecks across the full stack, from kernel and OS behavior to application-level code and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and product teams to understand both internal and customer use cases, and translate them into robust technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement new platform capabilities with a strong emphasis on measurable performance gains in real-world deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in daily stand-ups, release planning, and prioritization discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Sc. or M.Sc. in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience writing object-oriented C++ and/or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with embedded Linux systems, including cross-compilation, debugging, profiling, and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on background in diagnosing and optimizing real-world system behavior, including CPU, memory, I/O, networking, boot time, and application latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or optimizing low-latency video or data-streaming pipelines, ideally on embedded platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of software systems that span embedded devices, higher-level applications, and fully integrated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals, including system design, implementation, debugging, and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with video codecs, GStreamer, RTP/RTSP, or hardware-accelerated media pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Debian/Ubuntu-based systems, Bash scripting, and systemd.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker and docker-compose in complex development and deployment environments, as well as qemu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and performance analysis skills at both system and application level, combined with a proactive and self-directed working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in ROS2/DDS-style middleware and experienced with networking across multiple OSI layers, including REST APIs and performance-sensitive communication paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system integration and interfacing sensors or peripherals, especially via USB and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile engineering environment with stand-ups, sprint planning, and shared ownership across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with build systems such as CMake, including improving build performance in large-scale software projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
