r from now.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>The role</h2><p>You'll join our engineering team as a <strong>Senior Go Backend Developer</strong> and take real ownership of critical backend systems and services — not ticket-pushing, actual ownership.</p><p>You'll design, build, and evolve the backend services that power our products, weigh in on architectural decisions, improve system reliability, and help shape how backend engineering is done across the company.</p><p>This is a hands-on senior role: you'll write production Go every day and be deeply involved in technical decisions that have real impact.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h2>Quick reminder before the details</h2><p><strong>5+ years of production Go experience</strong> — required <strong>Based in a European timezone (UTC−1 to UTC+3)</strong> </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul><li><p>Design, build, and maintain backend services written in Go</p></li><li><p>Build and evolve APIs (GraphQL and/or REST) behind complex product workflows</p></li><li><p>Design scalable, reliable, and maintainable backend architectures</p></li><li><p>Work closely with frontend engineers, product managers, data engineers, and designers</p></li><li><p>Contribute to data modeling, business logic, and performance optimization</p></li><li><p>Review code and take part in architectural and technical discussions</p></li><li><p>Raise the bar on code quality, testing, observability, and system resilience</p></li><li><p>Actively tackle refactoring, technical debt, and long-term improvements</p></li><li><p>Own backend features end to end, from design to production</p></li><li><p>Take part in Agile ceremonies (planning, stand-ups, retrospectives)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>Our stack</h2><p>Go sits at the center of everything. Around it, you'll work with (and should be comfortable with):</p><ul><li><p>API design (GraphQL and/or REST)</p></li><li><p>PostgreSQL (or similar 