inienbusse zuverlässig unterwegs sind? <br><br>Dann könnte diese Stelle zu Dir passen! Per sofort oder nach Vereinbarung sucht Daimler Buses für die Werkstatt in Domdidier (Friboug) einen Automobil-Mechatroniker / Automobil-Fachmann in Festanstellung.<br><br>Du hast Erfahrung aus dem Automobilbereich, aber bisher noch nicht mit Bussen gearbeitet? Das ist kein Problem: Für Daimler Buses zählen vor allem die richtige Einstellung und die Bereitschaft, Dich rasch in neue Themen einzuarbeiten.<br>Bei dieser Stelle übernimmst Du folgende Tätigkeiten:<ul><li>Durchführen von Wartungs-, Reparatur- und Revisionsarbeiten an den von Daimler Buses betreuten Reise- und Linienbussen.</li><li>Diagnostizieren von Störungen sowie Prüfen und Instandsetzen mechanischer Fahrzeugkomponenten und elektronischer Systeme.</li><li>Aufbereiten von Neufahrzeugen.</li><li>Dokumentieren der ausgeführten Arbeiten.</li><li>Gelegentliche Übernahme des 24-Stunden-Bereitschaftsdienstes; dieser wird selbstverständlich zusätzlich vergütet.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Dein Profil</strong><p><ul><li>Abgeschlossene Berufsausbildung im Automobilbereich, zum Beispiel als Automobil-Mechatroniker EFZ oder Automobil-Fachmann EFZ. Eine Ausrichtung auf Nutzfahrzeuge ist von Vorteil, aber keine Voraussetzung.</li><li>Idealerweise einige Jahre Berufserfahrung; Erfahrung mit Bussen ist nicht zwingend erforderlich.</li><li>Gute Kenntnisse in Deutsch oder Französisch. Kenntnisse der jeweils anderen Sprache sind willkommen, aber keine Voraussetzung.</li><li>Selbstständige, belastbare und flexible Arbeitsweise sowie eine offene und teamorientierte Persönlichkeit.</li><li>Führerausweis der Kategorie C nicht zwingend erforderlich; Bereitschaft, diesen zu einem späteren Zeitpunkt zu erwerben.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Was unser Mandant bietet</strong><p>Bei Daimler Buses arbeitest Du mit Produkten der Premium-Klasse und hältst die Welt in Bewegung. Dich erwarten:<ul><li>eine 40-Stunden-Woche und fünf Wochen Ferien.</li><li>eine abwechslungsreiche und verantwortungsvolle Tätigkeit.</li><li>eine zusätzliche Vergütung für den gelegentlichen 24-Stunden-Bereitschaftsdienst.</li></ul></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/edl-consulting/daimler-buses-automobil-mechatroniker-automobil-fachmann-m-w-fur-nutzfahrzeuge-domdidier-fribourg-67712","tags":["Automobil-Mechatroniker EFZ","Automobil-Fachmann EFZ","Nutzfahrzeugtechnik","Busmechaniker","Reisebusse","Fahrzeugdiagnose"],"job_types":["Entry","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Domdidier","created_at":1791317394},{"slug":"senior-recruiting-specialist-remote-ch-schweiz-91744","company_name":"Edl Consulting","title":"(Senior) Recruiting Specialist (m/w/d) remote CH","description":"<br><strong>What to expect</strong><p><p>Are you an experienced recruiter with a hands-on mindset, accustomed to end-to-end recruiting in a fast-paced, dynamic environment—from job analysis to offer closure? Have you filled technical, functional, and commercial roles, communicate confidently with hiring managers and clients, and know exactly which levers move a role to a quick, high-quality hire?</p><p>Then you’re a fit for us. We’re not looking for an administrator of open roles, but a recruiting consultant who thinks ahead, advises, and delivers.</p></p><br><strong>Your tasks and responsibilities</strong><p><br><ul style="font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;color:rgb(0,0,0);"><li>You independently manage end-to-end recruiting mandates for our clients (SMEs, start-ups, scale-ups)—from requirements analysis to successful placement</li><li>You act as a sparring partner to our clients on job titles, job descriptions, recruiting strategies, channel selection, and market positioning</li><li>You conduct active search via LinkedIn Recruiter and other (AI-based) sourcing tools, proactively identifying and approaching suitable candidates</li><li>You carry out screening calls and qualifying first interviews in German, English, and ideally French</li><li>You own all candidate communication, including scheduling, candidate care, and process management in the ATS</li><li>You create compelling job descriptions, develop posting strategies, and implement them operationally</li><li>You produce project documentation, screening forms, candidate reports, and other materials for our clients</li><li>Where needed, you facilitate workshops and training sessions for our clients’ hiring managers and recruiters</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><br><ul style="font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;color:rgb(0,0,0);"><li>At least 5 years of recruiting experience—ideally in a start-up, scale-up, or high-volume environment with a fast pace and high autonomy</li><li>University degree in business administration, psychology, or a related field</li><li>Proven track record filling a broad spectrum of roles: technical positions (software, hardware, engineering), functional roles (HR, finance, operations), and sales &amp; marketing positions</li><li>Mastery of end-to-end recruiting; accustomed to independently steering mandates from the client intake session to offer</li><li>Excellent active search skills and routine use of LinkedIn Recruiter; experience with AI-based sourcing tools is a plus</li><li>Hands-on experience with various ATS/recruiting software systems (e.g., Personio, Successfactors, or similar) and quick to get up to speed in new tools</li><li>Confident, consultative communication with clients and hiring managers—you recommend the right strategy, not just the fastest</li><li>Highly productive, efficient, and structured working style; quick grasp of new concepts and strong process understanding</li><li>Tech-savvy and open to new tools, automations, and AI-supported workflows</li><li>Fluent written and spoken German and English; French is a strong plus</li><li>Based in Switzerland with the appropriate residence and work permits</li></ul></p><br><strong>Our offer</strong><p><br><ul><li><strong>Remote only:</strong> Work from wherever you’re most productive—on-site at the client only in exceptional cases; team events approx. once per quarter</li><li><strong>Maximum flexibility: </strong>Set your own working hours and achieve a healthy work–life balance</li><li><strong>Responsibility from day one: </strong>You run your own mandates and are a core part of our team—no hierarchy, short decision paths</li><li><strong>Variety and growth:</strong> No two mandates are alike—you recruit across industries, functions, and seniority levels and continuously develop your skills</li><li><strong>Appreciation:</strong> We value you as a team member and as a person—trust, coaching, and honest feedback are part of our culture</li></ul></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/edl-consulting/senior-recruiting-specialist-remote-ch-schweiz-91744","tags":["Recruiting","Applicant Management","Talent Aquisition","Coordination","HR"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full or part time"],"location":"Schweiz","created_at":1791317394},{"slug":"senior-automation-ot-engineer-n-e-visp-10834","company_name":"ten23 health AG","title":"Senior Automation & OT Engineer e/v/e/r/y/o/n/e","description":"<br><strong>About Us</strong><p><span style="color:rgb(66,66,66);font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif, Inter, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline;">ten23 health is a human-centric and sustainable strategic partner of choice for the pharmaceutical industry and biotech start-ups for the development, manufacture, and testing of tomorrow’s medicines. We support our clients in developing differentiated, stable, usable, and safe injecta